{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Compatibility"},"description":"Match two people's Vedic charts with Moon Dasha: Guna Milan (Ashtakoota) out of 36 with each koota's points, the koota doshas and the Muhurta Chintamani conditions that lift them; each person's Mangal Dosha (outside the 36); and Dual Cosmodyne, a Western synastry score with its strongest aspects. Each score stands on its own. Needs both people's birth dates, local birth times and birthplaces (place_ids from find_place). Guna Milan reads one person as the groom and one as the bride, so it needs to know who is the man and who is the woman: ask if the person has not said, and set groom to the man's letter. With no genders given, or for a couple of the same sex, person A takes the groom's seat. The figures are Moon Dasha's calculations. A score shows how two charts agree by tradition, not whether a relationship will succeed; never treat it as a reason not to marry, never read Nadi as a medical or genetic test, and never predict death, illness, a child's sex, markets, elections or court cases.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"aspect_descriptions":{"description":"Add a short description to each Dual Cosmodyne aspect listed. Set only when the person asks what the aspects mean.","type":"boolean"},"ayanamsa":{"description":"Default Lahiri. Krishnamurti is the KP ayanamsa.","enum":["Lahiri","TrueLahiri","Krishnamurti","Raman","Fagan","Yukteshwar","Galactic","Dhruva","Pushya","Ushashashi","ChandraHari","TrueRevati","SuryaSiddhanta","Tropical"],"type":"string"},"groom":{"description":"Which person takes the groom's seat in Guna Milan. Default a. Set b only when the person has said that B is the man in a man-and-woman couple.","enum":["a","b"],"type":"string"},"person_a":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"One person: birth date, local birth time